+++ b/serve/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# Serving DeepInfer + host prefix cache (local additions, not part of upstream)
+
+## Pieces
+
+- `serve/openai_server.py` — OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions` (streaming, `tools`, usage) on top of the
+  offline engine: one engine process per GPU (attention DP + MoE EP). `serve/server.sh start|stop` runs it as a
+  process group (stop reaps the engine helpers, which otherwise keep the GPUs).
+- `deepinfer/hicache/` — host-memory prefix cache (SGLang HiCache style): pinned host pools organized in pages
+  (one page = one 128-token KV block) plus SWA state slots, hash-chain index, LRU eviction, write-through at the
+  end of every prefill, "kernel" transfers (a CUDA kernel copying pages through UVA pointers on the engine
+  stream, `page_copy.cu`, JIT-built on first use). Needs the read-only `Sequence.block_table` binding added in
+  `csrc/engine/pybind_sequence.cpp` (rebuild `deepinfer._C` with `bash scripts/build.sh build`).
+- `tests/hicache/test_host_cache.py` — cache logic against a fake engine (needs one GPU).
+- `serve/check_prefix_cache.py` — A/B on a live server: each turn sent with `"prefix_cache": false` and with
+  the cache, greedy; compares outputs and TTFT.
+
+## Run
+
+```bash
+export DEEPINFER_ACCELERATOR=nvidia DEEPINFER_HF_MODEL_DIR=/path/to/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017
+serve/server.sh start --dp 4 --port 8888                       # cache on: 32 GiB pages + 4096 states per rank
+serve/server.sh start --dp 4 --port 8888 --hicache-size-gb 0   # cache off
+serve/server.sh start --dp 8 --cp 8 --max-num-seqs 32 --port 8888   # long context: one engine across 8 GPUs
+python serve/check_prefix_cache.py --port 8888 --turns 3
+curl -s localhost:8888/deepinfer/metrics | grep hicache         # per-rank hit/store counters
+serve/server.sh stop
+```
+
+`--dp` is the EP size (GPUs used) and `--cp` the context-parallel size, so the node runs `dp // cp`
+engines; `--max-num-seqs` is per engine, and with `--cp 8` there is one engine, so it bounds the whole
+node's concurrency. On 8x H20-3e a single 1M-token request takes 20.4 s to first token at `--cp 8`
+against 189 s at `--cp 1`, while `--cp 1` keeps ~34% more total throughput at 32 concurrent requests
+(notes/18-cp8-for-1m.md).
+
+### Protocol layer
+
+Request conversion, prompt rendering and output parsing are `deepseek-recipe`'s (the official Rust
+implementation, vendored in the image as `import deepseek_recipe`; `--protocol-layer recipe`, the
+default). The request becomes a `Conversation`, the conversation is rendered and encoded into token
+ids, and the engine's token ids go through a `StreamProcessor` that emits the protocol's own chunks.
+`--protocol-layer builtin` selects the older hand-written layer; `tools/recipe_parity.py` asserts the
+two agree on prompt text, token ids and parsed calls (see the serving notes).
+
+Endpoints: `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/messages` (Anthropic) and `/v1/responses`, all streaming or
+not, from the same engine. Usage carries the cache split in each protocol's own fields —
+`prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens` plus `prompt_cache_hit_tokens`/`prompt_cache_miss_tokens` for
+Chat Completions, `cache_read_input_tokens` for Messages — and `completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens`
+in thinking mode.
+
+### Image input
+
+`/v1/chat/completions` accepts OpenAI-style content parts. Each image becomes
+`<｜deepseek_image｜>` in the prompt, which `multi_modal_processor.overwrite_prompt` expands to the
+vision encoder's token grid, so `usage.prompt_tokens` counts the expanded tokens.
+
+```bash
+curl -s localhost:8888/v1/chat/completions -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{
+  "model": "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017",
+  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": [
+    {"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "data:image/jpeg;base64,<...>"}},
+    {"type": "text", "text": "describe this"}]}]}'
+```
+
+The block shape follows the endpoint: `{"type":"image_url","image_url":{"url":...}}` on
+`/v1/chat/completions`, `{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","data":...}}` on `/v1/messages`.
+A Messages-shaped image block sent to Chat Completions is rejected with 400, as the OpenAI schema
+says. Images may also sit inside a `tool_result` block. Multiple images per request keep their order.
+Only **inline base64 `data:` URLs** are allowed by default: this endpoint has no
+authentication, so fetching arbitrary URLs would turn it into an SSRF proxy. Pass
+`--allow-image-urls` to also accept `http(s)://` and local paths. Images are capped at 64 MiB and at
+`max_image_tokens` (1024) prompt tokens each; a request whose images cannot be decoded is rejected
+with 400 rather than silently degrading to text only.
+
+Knobs: `--hicache-size-gb`, `--hicache-state-slots`, `--routing affinity|least-loaded` (affinity keeps a
+conversation's turns on one rank, keyed by the first user message; required for hits since the cache is
+per rank). The cache requires decoder bounded replay (`--yoco-keep-tokens > 0`, the default 140).
+
+## How a hit works
+
+A new prompt's page hashes are matched from the start; the match is capped so that at least `keep_tokens`
+tokens remain to be recomputed (the decoder SWA state is rebuilt from that suffix by bounded replay), then
+snapped down to the nearest 128-aligned position that has a stored SWA state. The sequence is allocated up
+front, pages and state are copied in on the engine stream, `num_cached_tokens` is set, and the sequence is
+enqueued; the scheduler prefills only the suffix. Generated tokens are not stored at decode end (they are
+stored when they come back as part of the next turn's prompt).
+
+## AgentX
+
+The server speaks what InferenceX's AgentX replay (aiperf, `--endpoint /v1/chat/completions --streaming
+--use-server-token-count`) needs; `prefill-any-interval` matters there, since a single lane keeps most ranks idle.
